/T (When Battles Are Lost in a Chat.In the theater of alliance warfare, victory and defeat are often decided far from the battlefield. Our correspondent in the kingdom's chat has witnessed a tense exchange between the allegedly defeated King Orange and the cunning zunyah.The conflict centers on the defense of a capital. King Orange hides behind a supposed "game bug" and the lack of strong players to explain the defeat. However, zunyah doesn't buy the excuse, insisting that the responsibility lies with a lack of effort and the alliance's inability to recognize its own weakness.The tension escalates with accusations of "crying" and "arrogance," showing that in the chat, pride is just as valuable as any resource. In this realm, it's not enough to win; you also have to control the narrative. True power isn't in military might, but in who gets the last word. )
